  "noise_convention": "two-qubit REPLACEMENT depolarizing after every CNOT, on that CNOT's two wires: D_q(sigma) = (1-q) sigma + q [I_ij/4 (x) Tr_ij(sigma)]  -- NOT the 15-Pauli convention",
  "gate_sequence": "  1.  CNOT(q3 -> q4)   wires (2 -> 3)      [CNOT #1]  + depolarizing D_q on (2,3)\n  2.  CNOT(q2 -> q4)   wires (1 -> 3)      [CNOT #2]  + depolarizing D_q on (1,3)\n  3.  CNOT(q1 -> q4)   wires (0 -> 3)      [CNOT #3]  + depolarizing D_q on (0,3)\n  4.  CNOT(q3 -> q2)   wires (2 -> 1)      [CNOT #4]  + depolarizing D_q on (2,1)\n  5.  CNOT(q3 -> q1)   wires (2 -> 0)      [CNOT #5]  + depolarizing D_q on (2,0)\n  6.  H(q3)   wire 2      [ideal, no noise]\n  7.  measure (q3, q4) in the computational basis; success = (0, 0); retain (q1, q2)",
  "repeated_round_rule": "rho_n (x) rho_n -> noisy 5-CNOT circuit -> H(q3) -> postselect (q3,q4) = (0,0) -> trace out (q3,q4) -> normalise; the exact full 4x4 conditional state is fed into the next round",
